# VDE ARCHITECTURAL RECORD
# @shared-law (Forge Component)
# VDE Centralized Environment Secrets
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values.
# DO NOT COMMIT THE .env FILE.

# PostgreSQL Development Password
POSTGRES_DEV_PASSWORD=vde_dev_pass

# Projects base directory
# The base folder VDE creates a per-VM subfolder in (e.g. <base>/python, <base>/rust).
# Defaults to the in-tree VDE projects/ folder, but may point ANYWHERE you control,
# inside or outside VDE (e.g. $HOME/Projects). `vde init` prompts for this and writes
# the resolved ABSOLUTE path here. Leave unset to be prompted / accept the default.
# VDE_PROJECTS_DIR=

# Add other secrets here. They stay out of a Spoke's ENVIRONMENT: a Spoke container receives only
# VDE_AUTHORIZED_KEY (the public SSH key, written by vde itself) and
# POSTGRES_DEV_PASSWORD (the dev database password; the postgres and jupyterlab
# Spokes read it, and every Spoke's DATABASE_URL already carries it). A value a
# Spoke itself needs belongs in env-files/<alias>.env. Changes reach a Spoke when
# its container is recreated. The FILE itself is still readable inside a Spoke at /vde/.env
# (the repository is mounted there read-only); closing that is tracked in Issue #668.
